  "abstract": "<p>\n                    We prove the compatibility of local and global Langlands correspondences for\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G upper L Subscript n\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>G</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>L</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">GL_n</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    , which was proved up to semisimplification in M. Harris and R. Taylor,\n                    <italic>The Geometry and Cohomology of Some Simple Shimura Varieties</italic>\n                    , Ann. of Math. Studies 151, Princeton Univ. Press, Princeton-Oxford, 2001. More precisely, for the\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -dimensional\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"l\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">l</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -adic representation\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R Subscript l Baseline left-parenthesis normal upper Pi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                              Π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_l(\\Pi )</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    of the Galois group of an imaginary CM-field\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper L\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>L</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    attached to a conjugate self-dual regular algebraic cuspidal automorphic representation\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"normal upper Pi\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                            Π\n                            \n                          </mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Pi</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G upper L Subscript n Baseline left-parenthesis double-struck upper A Subscript upper L Baseline right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>G</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>L</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">A</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mi>L</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">GL_n(\\mathbb A_L)</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    , which is square integrable at some finite place, we show that Frobenius semisimplification of the restriction of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R Subscript l Baseline left-parenthesis normal upper Pi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                              Π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_l(\\Pi )</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    to the decomposition group of a place\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>v</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper L\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>L</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    not dividing\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"l\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">l</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    corresponds to\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"normal upper Pi Subscript v\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                              Π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mi>v</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:msub>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Pi _v</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    by the local Langlands correspondence. If\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"normal upper Pi Subscript v\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                              Π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mi>v</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:msub>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Pi _v</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is square integrable for some finite place\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v solidus vertical-bar l\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>v</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-REL\">\n                              <mml:mpadded width=\"0\">\n                                <mml:mtext>⧸</mml:mtext>\n                              </mml:mpadded>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mml:mo>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v \\not | l</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    we deduce that\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R Subscript l Baseline left-parenthesis normal upper Pi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                              Π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_l(\\Pi )</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is irreducible. We also obtain conditional results in the case\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v vertical-bar l\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>v</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mml:mo>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>l</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v|l</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    .\n                  </p>",
